+Quiz endpoints:
 
-## Getting Started
+- `POST /api/courses/{courseId}/quizzes` — create `{ "instructorId": 2, "title": "...", "questions": [{ "prompt": "...", "correctAnswer": "...", "points": 5 }] }`. The supplied instructor must own the course.
+- `GET /api/courses/{courseId}/quizzes` — list quizzes and public question fields (answer keys are omitted).
+- `POST /api/quizzes/{quizId}/grade` — submit `{ "studentId": 7, "answers": { "1": "A" }, "negativeMarking": false }`; saves a result and notifies registered observers.
 
-### Prerequisites
+The bundled backend uses an in-memory H2 database. Quiz results are persisted only for the lifetime of that database. Result observers currently write availability messages to the application log.
 
-- Java 17+  
-- Node.js 16+  
-- Angular CLI 16+  
-- Maven
